C:\Users/*
* Default wanted-item definitions used by bots to determine which items they should try to keep stocked or acquire.
*
* Each entry defines an item id, the minimum quantity that triggers demand, the quantity the bot should try to
* restock toward, and optional progression restrictions that control when the item is considered relevant.
*
* Item identifiers refer to both noted and unnoted variants, but all item IDs should use the unnoted variant.
*
* "min" is the quantity at which the bot begins wanting more of the item. -1 means the bot always wants more.
* "target" is the quantity the bot attempts to reach once restocking is triggered.
* "skill" identifies the relevant skill used for progression checks, or -1 for combat level.
* "max_level" is the level after which the item is no longer considered part of that progression tier, or -1 when
* there is no upper level restriction.
*
* Item-name comments beside each "id" are informational only and correspond to the item definitions in items.json.
*/

